  ["Problem five: search and sort. Binary search on a sorted slice with half-open bounds, then merge sort, the recursion every interviewer loves. And the one-liner from the library."] = "第 5 問: 探索とソート。半開区間でソート済み slice を二分探索、次に面接官が大好きな再帰、マージソート。そしてライブラリの 1 行版。",
  ["Problem four: the order queue as a singly linked list. Reverse it in place with three pointers, then detect a cycle with two runners of different speed."] = "第 4 問: 注文キューを単方向リストで。ポインタ 3 つでその場で反転し、速さの違う 2 つのランナーで循環を検出。",
  ["Problem seven, the one they always ask: N workers pull jobs from a channel and push results. Get the close and the wait in the right order and the job is yours."] = "第 7 問、必ず聞かれるやつ: N 個の worker が channel から jobs を取り、results を送る。close と wait の順番を正しくすれば内定はきみのもの。",
  ["Problem six: the classics. Two numbers that add up to the set price, a palindrome check that handles CJK, and whether two dish names are anagrams."] = "第 6 問: 定番問題。セット価格になる 2 つの数、CJK 対応の回文判定、そして 2 つの料理名がアナグラムかどうか。",
  ["Problem three: walk the MTR graph. Breadth-first with a queue for shortest hops, depth-first with recursion for reachability. Both need a visited set."] = "第 3 問: MTR のグラフを巡る。最短ホップはキューで幅優先、到達可能性は再帰で深さ優先。どちらも訪問済み set が要ります。",
  ["Problem two: a binary search tree of order numbers. Insert, walk in order, measure the height. In Go a tree is just a struct with two pointers and a nil at every leaf."] = "第 2 問: 注文番号の二分探索木。挿入し、順に巡回し、高さを測る。Go の木はポインタ 2 つを持つ struct と、葉ごとの nil にすぎません。",
  ["Pull a *RefundError out of the chain to read its fields. Fill: errors.___(err, &re)"] = "チェーンから *RefundError を取り出してフィールドを読みます。埋めてください: errors.___(err, &re)",
  ["Q other quest"] = "Q 別のクエスト",
  ["Q: "] = "Q: ",
  ["QUEST %d"] = "クエスト %d",
  ["R then Lock. Writers still use Lock and Unlock."] = "R の後に Lock。書き手は今まで通り Lock と Unlock です。",
  ["ROUND 1  -  the buzzer"] = "第1ラウンド  -  ブザー",
